EXPERIMENT 2 – EXPLORATORY TESTING ON INVENTORY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM

AIM
To perform exploratory testing on an inventory management system and identify and record software defects.

ALGORITHM
1. Open the inventory management system and explore its screens and features.
2. Prepare test charters for each testing session.
3. Test valid, invalid and unexpected inputs.
4. Explore product addition, stock updates, search, deletion and reports.
5. Record defects with reproduction steps and observations.
6. Review the testing notes and prepare a defect summary.

CODE
This is a manual testing experiment. No programming code is required.

INPUT
Feature	Test Input
Add product	Duplicate product code
Product price	Negative value
Stock update	Remove more stock than available
Search	Special characters
Delete product	Product used in an order
Login	Wrong user role URL

OUTPUT
Test	Defect Identified
Add product	Duplicate code accepted
Product price	Negative price saved
Stock update	Stock becomes negative
Search	Special characters cause error
Delete product	Ordered product can be deleted
Login	Unauthorized role page opens

RESULT
Thus, exploratory testing was performed on the inventory management system, and defects were identified and documented using test charters.
